  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-05-12T20:27:55.244Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "**Description**\n\nWhenever you unplug and then re-plug any USB device—especially the one your audio listening device is connected to—VRChat loses *world* audio. All non-world audio (Other users, avatar audio, menu sounds) continues unaffected. The only fix is to completely rejoin the world.\n\n---\n\n**Steps to Reproduce**\n\n1. Launch VRChat and join any populated world.\n\n2. Verify you can hear other users and ambient world sounds.\n\n3. Unplug a USB device (e.g. your audio interface or another USB peripheral).\n\n4. Wait ~5 seconds, then plug it back in.\n\n5. Observe that world audio is now silent.\n\n---\n\n**Actual Result**\n\n* **World audio**: completely dead.\n\n* **Other audio** (Menu sounds, other users, avatar audio): still playing.\n\n---\n\n**Expected Result**\n\nReconnecting a USB device should *not* terminate world audio. All sounds should continue seamlessly.\n\n---\n\n**Workaround**\n\nRejoining the world restores world audio.\n\n---\n\n**Additional Comments**\n\n In my case, the main USB hub most of my peripherals are connected to including my headphones occasionally disconnects and reconnects and this is when I notice the issue occurring. The issue seems to only occur in Desktop, not sure about VR.",
